{"id":"mahabharata-7-121","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":121,"title":"एकविंशत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 121 · Arjuna kills Jayadratha","summary":{"en":"Arjuna cuts through the Kaurava ranks toward Jayadratha, and as the sun sets he strikes off the head of the king and carries it away on his arrows. By Krishna's counsel the head falls into the lap of Jayadratha's father Vriddhakshatra, who is killed as his curse comes true.","kn":"ಅರ್ಜುನ ಜಯದ್ರಥನತ್ತ ಕೌರವ ಸಾಲುಗಳನ್ನು ಸೀಳಿ ಹೋಗಿ ಸೂರ್ಯಾಸ್ತದ ವೇಳೆ ರಾಜನ ತಲೆ ಕತ್ತರಿಸಿ ಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಒಯ್ಯುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕೃಷ್ಣನ ಸಲಹೆಯಂತೆ ತಲೆ ಜಯದ್ರಥನ ತಂದೆ ವೃದ್ಧಕ್ಷತ್ರನ ಮಡಿಲಲ್ಲಿ ಬೀಳುತ್ತದೆ; ಶಾಪದಂತೆ ಅವನು ಸಾಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अर्जुन कौरव पंक्तियों को चीरकर जयद्रथ तक पहुँचते हैं और सूर्यास्त के समय राजा का सिर काटकर बाणों से उड़ा ले जाते हैं। कृष्ण की सलाह से सिर जयद्रथ के पिता वृद्धक्षत्र की गोद में गिरता है और शाप के अनुसार वे मर जाते हैं।","te":"అర్జునుడు కౌరవ వరుసలను చీల్చుకుని జయద్రథుని వద్దకు వెళ్లి సూర్యాస్తమయ వేళ రాజు తలను నరికి బాణాలతో మోసుకెళతాడు. కృష్ణుని సలహాతో ఆ తల జయద్రథుని తండ్రి వృద్ధక్షత్రుని ఒడిలో పడుతుంది; శాపం ప్రకారం అతడు చస్తాడు.","ta":"அர்ஜுனன் கௌரவ அணிகளைப் பிளந்து ஜயத்ரதனை அடைந்து, சூரிய அஸ்தமன நேரத்தில் மன்னனின் தலையை வெட்டி அம்புகளால் கொண்டுசெல்கிறான். கண்ணனின் ஆலோசனைப்படி அத்தலை ஜயத்ரதனின் தந்தை வ்ருத்தக்ஷத்ரனின் மடியில் விழுந்து, சாபப்படி அவன் இறக்கிறான்.","ml":"സൂര്യാസ്തമയത്തിൽ കൗരവ നിരകളിലൂടെ അർജുനൻ ജയദ്രഥന്റെ നേർക്ക് മുന്നേറി രാജാവിന്റെ തല വെട്ടി അമ്പുകളിൽ കൊണ്ടുപോകുന്നു. കൃഷ്ണന്റെ ഉപദേശപ്രകാരം ആ തല ജയദ്രഥന്റെ പിതാവ് വൃദ്ധക്ഷത്രന്റെ മടിയിൽ വീഴുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ ശാപം ഫലിച്ച് വൃദ്ധക്ഷത്രനും കൊല്ലപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.121; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स रणे व्यचरत्पार्थः प्रेक्षणीयो धनंजयः ।\nयुगपद्दिक्षु सर्वासु चित्राण्यस्त्राणि दर्शयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha Dhananjaya ranged through the battle, a sight to behold, showing marvelous weapons at once in every direction."}},{"n":2,"text":"मध्यंदिनगतं सूर्यं प्रतपन्तमिवाम्बरे ।\nन शेकुः सर्वभूतानि पाण्डवं प्रतिवीक्षितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All creatures could not look at the Pandava, who blazed like the midday sun in the sky."}},{"n":3,"text":"प्रसृतांस्तस्य गाण्डीवाच्छरव्रातान्महात्मनः ।\nसंग्रामे समपश्याम हंसपङ्क्तीरिवाम्बरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that battle we saw the volleys of arrows flying from the great-souled man's Gandiva like lines of geese in the sky."}},{"n":4,"text":"विनिवार्य स वीराणामस्त्रैरस्त्राणि सर्वशः ।\nदर्शयन्रौद्रमात्मानमुग्रे कर्मणि धिष्ठितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Warding off the heroes' weapons everywhere with his own, he showed his fearsome self, set to terrible work."}},{"n":5,"text":"स तान्रथवरान्राजन्नभ्यतिक्रामदर्जुनः ।\nमोहयन्निव नाराचैर्जयद्रथवधेप्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna passed beyond those best of chariot-fighters, O king, seeming to bewilder them with his iron arrows, in his wish to kill Jayadratha."}},{"n":6,"text":"विसृजन्दिक्षु सर्वासु शरानसितसारथिः ।\nस रणे व्यचरत्तूर्णं प्रेक्षणीयो धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shooting arrows in all directions, the man of the white-horsed chariot, Dhananjaya, swiftly moved through the battle, a sight to see."}},{"n":7,"text":"भ्रमन्त इव शूरस्य शरव्राता महात्मनः ।\nअदृश्यन्तान्तरिक्षस्थाः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-souled hero's volleys of arrows seemed to whirl, and were seen in the air by hundreds and thousands."}},{"n":8,"text":"आददानं महेष्वासं संदधानं च पाण्डवम् ।\nविसृजन्तं च कौन्तेयं नानुपश्यामहे तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"We could not then see the Pandava great bowman taking up, fitting or loosing his arrows."}},{"n":9,"text":"तथा सर्वा दिशो राजन्सर्वांश्च रथिनो रणे ।\nआकुलीकृत्य कौन्तेयो जयद्रथमुपाद्रवत् ।\nविव्याध च चतुःषष्ट्या शराणां नतपर्वणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Throwing all the quarters and all the chariot-warriors into confusion, the son of Kunti rushed upon Jayadratha and struck him with sixty-four straight-jointed arrows."}},{"n":10,"text":"सैन्धवस्तु तथा विद्धः शरैर्गाण्डीवधन्वना ।\nन चक्षमे सुसंक्रुद्धस्तोत्त्रार्दित इव द्विपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pierced thus by arrows from the wielder of Gandiva, Saindhava could not bear it and, furious, was like an elephant goaded by a hook."}},{"n":11,"text":"स वराहध्वजस्तूर्णं गार्ध्रपत्रानजिह्मगान् ।\nआशीविषसमप्रख्यान्कर्मारपरिमार्जितान् ।\nमुमोच निशितान्संख्ये सायकान्सव्यसाचिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The man with the boar banner quickly loosed at Savyasachin sharp, straight arrows with vulture feathers, bright as venomous snakes and polished by the smith."}},{"n":12,"text":"त्रिभिस्तु विद्ध्वा गाण्डीवं नाराचैः षड्भिरर्जुनम् ।\nअष्टाभिर्वाजिनोऽविध्यद्ध्वजं चैकेन पत्रिणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced Gandiva with three iron arrows, Arjuna with six, the horses with eight, and the banner with one feathered shaft."}},{"n":13,"text":"स विक्षिप्यार्जुनस्तीक्ष्णान्सैन्धवप्रेषिताञ्शरान् ।\nयुगपत्तस्य चिच्छेद शराभ्यां सैन्धवस्य ह ।\nसारथेश्च शिरः कायाद्ध्वजं च समलंकृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna scattered the sharp arrows sent by Saindhava and at once cut with two arrows the charioteer's head from his body and the adorned banner."}},{"n":14,"text":"स छिन्नयष्टिः सुमहाञ्शीर्यमाणः शराहतः ।\nवराहः सिन्धुराजस्य पपाताग्निशिखोपमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its staff cut, the great boar banner of the Sindhu king, struck by arrows and shattered, fell like a flame."}},{"n":15,"text":"एतस्मिन्नेव काले तु द्रुतं गच्छति भास्करे ।\nअब्रवीत्पाण्डवं तत्र त्वरमाणो जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that moment, as the sun was moving quickly down, Janardana hurriedly spoke to the Pandava."}},{"n":16,"text":"धनंजय शिरश्छिन्धि सैन्धवस्य दुरात्मनः ।\nअस्तं महीधरश्रेष्ठं यियासति दिवाकरः ।\nशृणुष्वैव च मे वाक्यं जयद्रथवधं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dhananjaya, cut off the head of wicked Saindhava! The sun is about to go to the best of mountains, the setting one. Listen to my words about killing Jayadratha."}},{"n":17,"text":"वृद्धक्षत्रः सैन्धवस्य पिता जगति विश्रुतः ।\nस कालेनेह महता सैन्धवं प्राप्तवान्सुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vriddhakshatra, Saindhava's father, is famed in the world. After a long time he got this son Saindhava."}},{"n":18,"text":"जयद्रथममित्रघ्नं तं चोवाच ततो नृपम् ।\nअन्तर्हिता तदा वाणी मेघदुन्दुभिनिस्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as he was telling that enemy-slayer King Jayadratha, an unseen voice rumbling like thunder-clouds and drums said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"तवात्मजोऽयं मर्त्येषु कुलशीलदमादिभिः ।\nगुणैर्भविष्यति विभो सदृशो वंशयोर्द्वयोः ।\nक्षत्रियप्रवरो लोके नित्यं शूराभिसत्कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'This son of yours, lord, will be among mortals equal in good birth, conduct, self-control and other qualities to both his families, and will be a foremost warrior always honored by heroes."}},{"n":20,"text":"शत्रुभिर्युध्यमानस्य संग्रामे त्वस्य धन्विनः ।\nशिरश्छेत्स्यति संक्रुद्धः शत्रुर्नालक्षितो भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"But while this bowman is fighting enemies in battle, an enemy unseen on earth, in anger, will cut off his head.'"}},{"n":21,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा सिन्धुराजो ध्यात्वा चिरमरिंदम ।\nज्ञातीन्सर्वानुवाचेदं पुत्रस्नेहाभिपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, the Sindhu king thought for a long time, O scourge of foes, and, pained by love for his son, said to all his kinsmen:"}},{"n":22,"text":"संग्रामे युध्यमानस्य वहतो महतीं धुरम् ।\nधरण्यां मम पुत्रस्य पातयिष्यति यः शिरः ।\nतस्यापि शतधा मूर्धा फलिष्यति न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Whoever, as my son fights and bears a great burden in battle, makes his head fall to the ground, that man's head too will split into a hundred pieces, without doubt.'"}},{"n":23,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततो राज्ये स्थापयित्वा जयद्रथम् ।\nवृद्धक्षत्रो वनं यातस्तपश्चेष्टं समास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, Vriddhakshatra set Jayadratha on the throne and went to the forest, devoted to austerities."}},{"n":24,"text":"सोऽयं तप्यति तेजस्वी तपो घोरं दुरासदम् ।\nसमन्तपञ्चकादस्माद्बहिर्वानरकेतन ॥","meaning":{"en":"That radiant man now performs fearful and unapproachable austerities, O man of the monkey banner, outside this Samantapanchaka."}},{"n":25,"text":"तस्माज्जयद्रथस्य त्वं शिरश्छित्त्वा महामृधे ।\nदिव्येनास्त्रेण रिपुहन्घोरेणाद्भुतकर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, Arjuna, slayer of foes, cut off Jayadratha's head in this great battle with a divine weapon, terrible and of wondrous action,"}},{"n":26,"text":"सकुण्डलं सिन्धुपतेः प्रभञ्जनसुतानुज ।\nउत्सङ्गे पातयस्वाशु वृद्धक्षत्रस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"and quickly make that head, with its earrings, fall into the lap of Vriddhakshatra, O Bharata, younger brother of Wind's son."}},{"n":27,"text":"अथ त्वमस्य मूर्धानं पातयिष्यसि भूतले ।\nतवापि शतधा मूर्धा फलिष्यति न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you make his head fall to the ground, yours too will split into a hundred pieces, without doubt."}},{"n":28,"text":"यथा चैतन्न जानीयात्स राजा पृथिवीपतिः ।\nतथा कुरु कुरुश्रेष्ठ दिव्यमस्त्रमुपाश्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So do it, best of the Kurus, with a divine weapon, so that this king, lord of the earth, does not know it."}},{"n":29,"text":"न ह्यसाध्यमकार्यं वा विद्यते तव किंचन ।\nसमस्तेष्वपि लोकेषु त्रिषु वासवनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"For nothing is impossible or beyond you, Indra's son, in all three worlds.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा तु वचनं सृक्किणी परिसंलिहन् ।\nइन्द्राशनिसमस्पर्शं दिव्यमन्त्राभिमन्त्रितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, Arjuna licked the corners of his mouth and quickly loosed an arrow, set on killing Saindhava, one with the touch of Indra's thunderbolt, charged with divine mantras,"}},{"n":31,"text":"सर्वभारसहं शश्वद्गन्धमाल्यार्चितं शरम् ।\nविससर्जार्जुनस्तूर्णं सैन्धवस्य वधे वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"able to bear every burden, always honored with perfume and garlands."}},{"n":32,"text":"स तु गाण्डीवनिर्मुक्तः शरः श्येन इवाशुगः ।\nशकुन्तमिव वृक्षाग्रात्सैन्धवस्य शिरोऽहरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Loosed from Gandiva, that arrow flew like a swift hawk and took Saindhava's head as a hawk takes a bird from a treetop."}},{"n":33,"text":"अहरत्तत्पुनश्चैव शरैरूर्ध्वं धनंजयः ।\nदुर्हृदामप्रहर्षाय सुहृदां हर्षणाय च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Dhananjaya with more arrows kept carrying it upward, to the dismay of his enemies and delight of his friends."}},{"n":34,"text":"शरैः कदम्बकीकृत्य काले तस्मिंश्च पाण्डवः ।\nसमन्तपञ्चकाद्बाह्यं शिरस्तद्व्यहरत्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that time the Pandava, driving it on with a stream of arrows, carried that head outside Samantapanchaka."}},{"n":35,"text":"एतस्मिन्नेव काले तु वृद्धक्षत्रो महीपतिः ।\nसंध्यामुपास्ते तेजस्वी संबन्धी तव मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that very moment King Vriddhakshatra, your relative, honorable sir, the radiant one, was at his evening prayers."}},{"n":36,"text":"उपासीनस्य तस्याथ कृष्णकेशं सकुण्डलम् ।\nसिन्धुराजस्य मूर्धानमुत्सङ्गे समपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he sat so, the head of the Sindhu king, with black hair and earrings, was made to fall into his lap."}},{"n":37,"text":"तस्योत्सङ्गे निपतितं शिरस्तच्चारुकुण्डलम् ।\nवृद्धक्षत्रस्य नृपतेरलक्षितमरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lovely-earringed head fell into King Vriddhakshatra's lap without his noticing, O scourge of foes."}},{"n":38,"text":"कृतजप्यस्य तस्याथ वृद्धक्षत्रस्य धीमतः ।\nउत्तिष्ठतस्तत्सहसा शिरोऽगच्छद्धरातलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the wise Vriddhakshatra finished his recitation and suddenly stood up, the head fell to the ground."}},{"n":39,"text":"ततस्तस्य नरेन्द्रस्य पुत्रमूर्धनि भूतलम् ।\nगते तस्यापि शतधा मूर्धागच्छदरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, when his son's head reached the ground, his own head, O scourge of foes, split into a hundred pieces."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततः सर्वाणि भूतानि विस्मयं जग्मुरुत्तमम् ।\nवासुदेवश्च बीभत्सुं प्रशशंस महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all beings were filled with great amazement, and Vasudeva praised the great chariot-fighter Bibhatsu."}},{"n":41,"text":"ततो दृष्ट्वा विनिहतं सिन्धुराजं जयद्रथम् ।\nपुत्राणां तव नेत्रेभ्यो दुःखाद्बह्वपतज्जलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Jayadratha the Sindhu king dead, your sons shed many tears from their eyes in grief."}},{"n":42,"text":"भीमसेनोऽपि संग्रामे बोधयन्निव पाण्डवम् ।\nसिंहनादेन महता पूरयामास रोदसी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena too, as though waking the Pandava, filled heaven and earth with a great lion's roar in the battle."}},{"n":43,"text":"तं श्रुत्वा तु महानादं धर्मपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nसैन्धवं निहतं मेने फल्गुनेन महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that great roar, Yudhishthira, the son of Dharma, thought that Saindhava had been killed by great-souled Phalguna."}},{"n":44,"text":"ततो वादित्रघोषेण स्वान्योधानभिहर्षयन् ।\nअभ्यवर्तत संग्रामे भारद्वाजं युयुत्सया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, delighting his own warriors with the sound of instruments, he advanced into battle against Bharadvaja's son, eager to fight."}},{"n":45,"text":"ततः प्रववृते राजन्नस्तं गच्छति भास्करे ।\nद्रोणस्य सोमकैः सार्धं संग्रामो लोमहर्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, as the sun was setting, a hair-raising battle began between Drona and the Somakas."}},{"n":46,"text":"ते तु सर्वप्रयत्नेन भारद्वाजं जिघांसवः ।\nसैन्धवे निहते राजन्नयुध्यन्त महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Eager to kill Bharadvaja's son, those great chariot-fighters, though Saindhava was dead, fought him with all effort."}},{"n":47,"text":"पाण्डवास्तु जयं लब्ध्वा सैन्धवं विनिहत्य च ।\nअयोधयंस्ततो द्रोणं जयोन्मत्तास्ततस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas, having won victory and killed Saindhava, drunk with victory, fought Drona here and there."}},{"n":48,"text":"अर्जुनोऽपि रणे योधांस्तावकान्रथसत्तमान् ।\nअयोधयन्महाराज हत्वा सैन्धवकं नृपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna too, O great king, after killing King Saindhava, fought your best chariot-warriors in battle."}},{"n":49,"text":"स देवशत्रूनिव देवराजः\nकिरीटमाली व्यधमत्समन्तात् ।\nयथा तमांस्यभ्युदितस्तमोघ्नः\nपूर्वां प्रतिज्ञां समवाप्य वीरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the lord of the gods scatters the gods' enemies, Kiritin scattered them on all sides, as the dispelling sun at its rising scatters the darkness, the hero having fulfilled his earlier vow."}}]}]}